Debug.Assert(OLD(Count) = RET, "The ArrayList should have the same count before and after adding elements");
</code>
The assert statement corresponds to the comment that starts with "@@@". This comment asserts that the count of the ArrayList should be the same before and after adding elements. The assertion uses the old value of the ArrayList's Count (stored as OLD(Count)) and compares it to the return value of the method (stored as RET). The result is a statement that asserts that the array list count before any modifications should be equal to the return value after adding elements.--------------------
Debug.Assert(RET - y == x); 
